{"artifact_reads":[{"digest_matched":true,"path":".gnd-planning/milestones/cross-document-growth/notes/cross-document-growth-plan.md"}],"concern_count":"7","disposition":"revise","reviewer_id":"glm","schema_version":2,"summary":"Digest verified. The r1 plan binds CG1-CG3 to the issue requirements with mostly falsifiable acceptance cases, and the referenced phase-CG1-spec.md supplies prefix/CAS ordering plus citation and uniqueness refusal cases. Two issue-339 aspects are not demonstrable as written: the consolidation loop's stopping condition rests on an undefined 'configured threshold' with no acceptance case exercising halting, and atomic apply of row moves together with role rewrites is specified only at preview. Ownership refusal, duplicate-append semantics, and the conditional status of the CG1 exit criterion against the open §10 storage decision also need tightening before implementation."}
{"concern_id":"cg3-loop-termination-undefined","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/cross-document-growth/notes/cross-document-growth-plan.md","location":"§2 line 19 and §4 line 31","observation":"Both state 'recompute candidates after apply and stop at the configured threshold', but no threshold is named or defined anywhere in the plan: it does not say what quantity is bounded (candidate score, review rounds, or work units), its default, or its configuration surface. A grep of src/gnd/evolve/ — the component set named in §3 line 23 — finds zero occurrences of 'threshold', so no existing configuration is being referenced either."},{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/cross-document-growth/notes/cross-document-growth-plan.md","location":"§6 line 41 and §9 line 57","observation":"§6 only says generically 'Record work counters and the first refusal where limits apply', and the CG3 acceptance cases in §9 are 'accept one group, decline another, restart from the decision log and verify that the declined group is not offered again unless its evidence changes' — decision persistence only; no case exercises the loop halting or a limit refusal."}],"recommendation":"In the CG3 spec, name the threshold's quantity, default and configuration key, and add a §9 falsifiable case in which recompute keeps yielding eligible groups (for example a chain of similar types where each accepted merge exposes a new candidate) and assert the loop stops at the bound with the first refusal recorded.","relevance":"blocking","severity":"high","title":"Consolidation loop termination rests on an undefined 'configured threshold' and no acceptance case exercises halting"}
{"concern_id":"cg3-apply-atomicity-unspecified","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/cross-document-growth/notes/cross-document-growth-plan.md","location":"§2 line 19 and §4 line 31","observation":"'Preview row moves and role rewrites together' binds only the preview; neither section states that apply performs the row moves and the role rewrites as one atomic, digest-bound unit, nor what is observable when one half is refused after the other has been staged. CG1 in contrast binds apply explicitly at §0 line 7: 'Document and check every new sample span against the cited document before CAS.'"},{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/cross-document-growth/notes/cross-document-growth-plan.md","location":"§9 line 57","observation":"The only related check is post-hoc and covers different operations: 'After a rename or deletion validate all role references and locate every transferred row's original source.' No case asserts an unchanged model when one half of a consolidation apply is refused."}],"recommendation":"State in §2/§4 that a consolidation apply is a single CAS covering rows and roles together and that any refusal leaves the model byte-identical (mirroring the CG1 stale-preview rule in the spec), and add a §9 case in which the role rewrite is refused after the row moves are staged, asserting the model is unchanged.","relevance":"blocking","severity":"high","title":"Atomic apply of row moves with role rewrites is specified only at preview, not at apply"}
