{"concern_id":"cg1-duplicate-append-semantics-open","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/cross-document-growth/notes/cross-document-growth-plan.md","location":"§0 line 7 and §6 line 41","observation":"'Count duplicate evidence separately from distinct rows' is asserted as a binding design rule in both sections."},{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/cross-document-growth/notes/cross-document-growth-plan.md","location":"§2 line 15 and §10 line 61","observation":"'Keep prior rows and spans intact' permits a retried or repeated apply to append the same located rows twice; the plan states no idempotency rule for apply. Meanwhile §10 leaves storage open — 'Choose append-only in-model storage or the external population requested in #338' — and the referenced phase-CG1-spec.md §6 says 'Identical rows with distinct supporting documents need an explicit provenance ruling' deferred under that open decision D1, so the binding counting rule presupposes an answer the plan itself marks unresolved."}],"recommendation":"State whether apply is idempotent for repeated identical located rows, and either detach the identical-rows-from-distinct-documents ruling from the §10 storage decision or mark §0's counting rule conditional on it; add a §9 case that applies the same located rows twice and asserts the counted outcome.","relevance":"hardening","severity":"medium","title":"Duplicate-observation counting is asserted as binding while identical-row provenance and apply idempotency are unresolved"}
